<div style="background-color: #1a5276; color: white; padding: 15px; text-align: center; border-radius: 8px; margin-bottom: 20px;">
    <h1 style="margin: 0;">Lesson Planner – Theme # ___ – Lesson # 3</h1>
    <p style="margin: 5px 0 0 0; font-size: 1.1em;">Complete this planner five times per theme, once per lesson (Lesson 1 through Lesson 5).</p>
</div>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Lesson #:</b> 3</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Skills Focus:</b> Speaking</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Grade:</b> 10th Grade (CEFR: B1.1)</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Scenario:</b> Future Plans and Time Capsule</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Theme:</b> How I Am Preparing for the Next Five Years</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;"><b>Date(s):</b> From ___ to ___</td>
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="2"><b>Learning Sequence Time:</b> 45–50 min</td>
    </tr>
    <tr style="border: 1px dashed #333;">
        <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;" colspan="3">
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Specific Objective:</b> Speaking: Productive: Explain how to use common technological devices and applications. Interactive: Exchange opinions about the results of surveys and investigations.</p>
            <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Learning Outcome:</b> Speaking: Can explain to classmates how to use a device to record goals for a time capsule (e.g., "Press this button to start recording."). Can exchange ideas about future goals and skills for career planning (e.g., "I think critical thinking will be important for my career."). Can discuss future career trends by sharing survey results and personal views related to Panama (e.g., "According to our class survey, many students want to pursue careers in tourism and eco-friendly innovation, which reflects Panama's focus on environmental conservation.").</p>
        </td>
    </tr>
</table>

<h2 style="color: #1a5276; text-align: center;">The Six Action-Oriented Approach (AOA) Lesson Stages</h2>

<table style="border: 1px dashed #333; border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 10px 0;">
    <thead>
        <tr style="background-color: #f2f2f2;">
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 33%; color: #1a5276;">Stage & Description</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 33%; color: #1a5276;">Activities & Teacher Actions</th>
            <th style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px; width: 33%; color: #1a5276;">Estimated Date and Time</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 1 — Warm-up / Pre-task</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Engagement, Modeling and Clarification of the lesson's main goal.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Warm-up:</b> The teacher starts by displaying images of various technological devices (e.g., a smartphone, a laptop, a virtual reality headset) and asks students to briefly discuss in pairs: "Which device do you think will be most important for future careers, and why?" or "If you could put one technological device in a time capsule to represent today, what would it be and why?" Students quickly share their answers with the class, activating vocabulary related to technology, future, and careers.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Modeling:</b> The teacher models how to express future plans and possibilities using modals and future continuous. For example, the teacher might say: "In five years, I <b>will be working</b> on educational technology projects. I <b>might pursue</b> a degree in software development. My former professor <b>said that I should</b> focus on critical thinking skills." The teacher also explicitly models the pronunciation of the long vowel /iː/ in words like "achieve," "believe," "volunteer," and "engineering," and stress in "leadership" and "critical thinking."</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Clarification (CCQs):</b> The teacher checks understanding of future plans and the concept of 'time capsule' verbally.
                    <ul>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"Are we discussing things that happened yesterday or things that will happen in the future?" (Expected answer: "Future.")</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"If I put a message in a time capsule, is it for now or for someone to find later?" (Expected answer: "For later, in the future.")</li>
                    </ul>
                </p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: center; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">5-7 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 2 — Presentation</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Input of new language/content connected to Scenario: "Future Plans and Time Capsule".</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Material:</b> The teacher presents a short audio excerpt (e.g., 2-3 minutes) from a podcast or an interview where two high school students from Panama discuss their future plans, career aspirations, and what they would include in a time capsule. The material will specifically feature phrases using modals for possibilities, future continuous, and reported speech. The scenario centers on them explaining how they would record their goals using a modern device.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Genre, register, and format:</b> Informal dialogue/podcast excerpt between two teenagers, conversational.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Competence:</b> Engages in conversational exchanges to discuss future plans, share opinions, and explain simple instructions related to technology.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Comprehension tasks:</b> Students listen to the audio and answer gist questions to understand the main ideas and target language.
                    <ul>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What are the main future goals discussed by the students?"</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What advice did one student mention receiving about career planning?"</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"How do they suggest recording their goals for the time capsule?"</li>
                    </ul>
                </p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: center; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">8-10 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 3 — Preparation / Practice</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Accuracy focus on Speaking.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Communicative Skill & Content:</b> Students practice using modals for career possibilities ("I might pursue...", "I could develop..."), future continuous for ongoing plans ("I will be working as...", "They will be gaining..."), and reported speech to share advice ("My teacher said that I should...", "My parents recommended that I..."). Focus on target vocabulary: <i>career, future, goals, possibilities, advice, education, technology, engineering, software developer, critical thinking, community service, opportunities, pursue, accomplish, reflect, suggest, recommend, develop, enhance.</i> Pronunciation practice of long /iː/ sounds and stress in multisyllabic words is integrated throughout.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Detailed Procedure:</b>
                    <ol>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Controlled Practice - Sentence Builder:</b> Students work individually to complete sentences orally using given prompts. The teacher provides sentence beginnings and vocabulary, and students complete them aloud, focusing on correct grammar and pronunciation. For example: "In five years, I _____ (study/engineering)." (Expected: "I will be studying engineering.") "My counselor _____ (suggest/develop/leadership skills)." (Expected: "My counselor suggested that I develop leadership skills.")</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Semi-controlled Practice - Chain Speaking:</b> In small groups, students take turns adding a sentence to a chain, building on the previous one. The first student states a future goal, the next adds a possibility using a modal, and the third shares a piece of advice using reported speech. Example: S1: "I will be working as a software developer." S2: "I might pursue an internship to gain experience." S3: "My friend said that I should volunteer for community service to enhance my skills."</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;"><b>Pair Interaction - "Future Talk":</b> Students work in pairs to ask and answer questions about their future goals and how they are preparing. They use wh-questions and try to incorporate at least one modal, one future continuous phrase, and one piece of reported advice in their conversation. Example questions: "What will you be doing to achieve your career goals in the next five years?" "What advice have you received about pursuing a high-demand career?" "How might technology help you develop your critical thinking skills?" Peers listen and provide feedback on language use and pronunciation, particularly focusing on the long /iː/ sound and word stress.</li>
                    </ol>
                </p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: center; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">15-18 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 4 — Performance / Production</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Communicative task where students USE the language in a realistic scenario: "Future Plans and Time Capsule".</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Task Format:</b> Group Discussion and Presentation – "Our Class Time Capsule: Future Goals & Skills." Students work in groups of 3-4. Each group is tasked with discussing what three future goals and associated skills they would collectively decide to record for a class time capsule to be opened in five years. They must also explain how they would digitally record these goals using a hypothetical device (e.g., "Press this button to start recording our career aspirations").</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Procedure:</b>
                    <ul>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">In their groups, students discuss potential goals and skills, using phrases like "I think critical thinking will be important for my career," "We might include a goal about pursuing eco-friendly innovation," or "According to our discussion, many students want to develop leadership skills." They also exchange ideas about career trends in Panama.</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Students explain how they would use a common technological device (e.g., a voice recorder app on a tablet, a video message function) to capture their goals for the time capsule. (e.g., "First, you need to turn on the tablet. Then, open the 'Future Me' app. Press this button to start recording our goals. We will be discussing how to achieve success in a high-demand field.")</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">They assign roles within the group (e.g., one recorder to note key points, one presenter to summarize, one timekeeper).</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Each group briefly presents their chosen goals, skills, and recording method to the class, using the target vocabulary, modals, future continuous, and reported speech.</li>
                    </ul>
                </p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Focus:</b> Fluency, collaborative interaction, clear explanation, and appropriate use of target language to complete the communicative task.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: center; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">10-12 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 5 — Assessment / Post-task</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Formative assessment strategy.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Formative Assessment Strategy:</b> Teacher Observation Checklist and Peer Assessment. The teacher observes groups during their discussions and presentations, using a checklist to note the use of target grammar, vocabulary, and pronunciation. Peers also provide feedback to other groups using a simple rubric focusing on clarity and language use.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Assessment Task:</b> Each group presents their "Time Capsule" plan to the class, explaining their selected goals, the skills required, and the steps to digitally record them. They are assessed on their ability to explain, exchange opinions, and use the target language effectively.</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Evaluation Criteria:</b>
                    <ul>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Intelligible pronunciation of target sounds (e.g., long /iː/ in "achieve," "leadership") and correct stress in multisyllabic words (e.g., "critical thinking," "community service").</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Appropriate use of target vocabulary (e.g., <i>career, goals, opportunities, pursue, develop, critical thinking</i>).</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Correct application of modals for possibilities (<i>might, could</i>), future continuous (<i>will be working</i>), and reported speech (<i>said that I should</i>).</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Clarity and coherence in explaining how to use a device and discussing future plans.</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">Effective collaboration and interaction within the group.</li>
                    </ul>
                </p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Assessment / Exit Ticket:</b> Students complete a brief reflection.
                    <ul>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"How well did I explain my future goals and how to record them using the new vocabulary and grammar?"</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What was challenging about exchanging opinions on future career trends, and how did I overcome it?"</li>
                    </ul>
                </p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: center; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">7-8 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <h3 style="color: #1a5276; margin-top: 0;">STAGE 6 — Reflection</h3>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">Review of the lesson and preparation for the next stage.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Student Self-Reflection Prompt:</b> Students reflect on their learning and participation.
                    <ul>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"What new speaking skills or vocabulary did I practice today that will help me talk about my future plans confidently?"</li>
                        <li style="margin-bottom: 4px; text-align: justify;">"How can discussing future plans and advice with my peers help me in my actual career planning process?"</li>
                    </ul>
                </p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Teacher Reflection:</b> The teacher considers: "Did students effectively use modals, future continuous, and reported speech to discuss their future plans and advice? Was the time capsule scenario engaging and effective in promoting interaction? Were there any specific pronunciation challenges (e.g., long /iː/ or word stress) that need further attention? What adjustments or additional scaffolds might be needed for students who struggled to express their ideas clearly?"</p>
                <p style="text-align: justify; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;"><b>Connection to next lesson:</b> This speaking lesson provided students with ample opportunity to verbalize their future plans, career aspirations, and the skills they need to develop. The ideas and language generated in today's discussions will serve as a direct foundation for Lesson 4 (Writing Composition), where students will construct well-structured paragraphs describing their individual five-year career plans and the steps they will take to achieve them, further embedding the vocabulary and grammatical structures practiced today.</p>
            </td>
            <td style="border: 1px dashed #333; padding: 8px;">
                <p style="text-align: center; margin: 4px 0 8px 0;">5 min</p>
            </td>
        </tr>
    </tbody>
</table>